+++ b/docs/csv_export.rst
@@ -45,6 +45,24 @@ The following options can be used to customize the CSVs returned by Datasette.
 ``?_dl=on``
     Causes Datasette to return a ``content-disposition: attachment; filename="filename.csv"`` header.
 
+``?_null=TEXT``
+    Use ``TEXT`` to represent SQL ``NULL`` values, for example ``?_null=NULL``.
+    If this parameter is omitted or empty (``?_null=``), ``NULL`` values are
+    exported as empty fields, as before. Empty strings, zero and other non-NULL
+    values are not replaced. This option only affects CSV, not JSON row data.
+
+    This works with table, view and custom SQL query exports, including every
+    page of ``?_stream=1`` exports and exports using ``?_header=off``. With
+    ``?_labels=1``, a NULL foreign key uses the marker in both its value and
+    label columns. NULL labels also use the marker, but labels that are actual
+    empty strings remain empty.
+
+    The marker can contain Unicode, commas, quotes and newlines. URL-encode
+    these characters in the query string (for example, ``%2C`` for a comma,
+    ``%22`` for a quote and ``%0A`` for a newline). Normal CSV quoting and
+    escaping is applied automatically, and ``?_trace=1`` also applies the
+    usual HTML escaping.
+
